{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["He said, <b>“My teaching shall drop as the rain”</b> — for that which he has taken from the heavens, even His word upon the earth, shall drop upon Israel and distill upon them like dew, as it says, “For the name of YHWH I call; ascribe greatness to our Elohim” (Deuteronomy 32:3) in the heavens — “Give greatness to our Elohim” upon the earth, and He speaks with all Israel. And likewise “the stone of Yehoshua” hints at this earth, for “from there the Shepherd, the Stone of Israel” (Genesis 49:24), and I have already explained this. And likewise, “The stone which the builders rejected has become the chief corner-stone; this is from YHWH” and so forth (Psalms 118:22–23). Therefore Yehoshua said (Joshua 24:27), “This stone shall be a witness among us,” and likewise, “For behold the stone that I have set before Yehoshua, upon one stone seven eyes” and so forth (Zechariah 3:9). And the enlightened will understand:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The verse quotations 'For the name of YHWH I call / ascribe greatness to our Elohim' are from Deuteronomy 32:3, which Ramban implicitly cites here; the Hebrew text does not mark the verse reference explicitly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:46.829813709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}